  "emotionDefinitions": {
    "anger": "Irritation through to rage. (Hall and Van de Castle)",
    "apprehension": "Fear, anxiety, guilt or embarrassment caused by a perceived threat of harm, punishment or social rejection. (Hall and Van de Castle)",
    "sadness": "Any unhappy emotional state, not physical pain. (Hall and Van de Castle)",
    "confusion": "Cognitive uncertainty or bewilderment, often from unexpected events or difficulty choosing. (Hall and Van de Castle)",
    "happiness": "Any pleasant feeling, from mild contentment to elation. (Hall and Van de Castle)",
    "wonder": "Awe, curiosity or nostalgia. Our addition; counts as happiness in Hall and Van de Castle terms."
  },
